Expiring articles based on number wouldn't work here. There are
certain groups critical to our purpose as a computer science
department, for example the comp.lang groups, which we want to keep
for as long as possible even if only one or two people use them. On
the other hand, "entertainment" groups, no matter how popular, are
expired as necessary to keep the disk from overflowing, which means we
do it by volume. 

  We are a small enough site that we are able to take requests to
extend the time of the popular groups, with the exception of the
alt.binaries.pics groups which are just TOO large for us to hold. 

I guess the bigger issue is the purpose of the site. As an academic
department, we don't have a problem ranking our priorities, but we
still try to carry everything. If we were a general university site,
or a business, or a pay-for-news public access site, we'd have
different values.


